cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this tool or these data, please cite the archived release."
title: "What Do Zero-Data Self-Play Models Add Beyond an Off-the-Shelf Compressor? A Byte-by-Byte Test: manuscript, scoring tool and per-byte compressor log losses"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-30
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23058002
repository-code: "https://github.com/lgboim/beyond-compressor"
abstract: >-
  Per-byte paq8px and lpaq1 log losses on the evaluation windows of Self-Play Pretraining with Zero Data, a tool that
  scores the realized gain of any byte-level model beyond these compressors under sequential fixed-share and exact
  Bayesian mixtures, and the manuscript reporting that the released self-play learners realize little gain beyond
  paq8px on text, code and formal data.
keywords:
  - zero-data pretraining
  - self-play
  - byte-level language models
  - lossless compression
  - context mixing
  - forecast combination
  - evaluation methodology
authors:
